---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../layouts/PageHead.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Payment & refund policy"
  description="How payment works at Shri Govardhan Goshala, and what to do if something went wrong."
>
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Payment & refunds"
    lede="Donations are not refundable — but mistakes happen, and here is exactly what to do." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--tight prose legal">
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated 11 August 2026</p>

      <h2>1. How you can pay</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>UPI only.</strong> Scan the QR code with any UPI app, tap
        through to your app from the payment page, or copy our UPI ID
        <code>{site.upi.vpa}</code> and pay from your own app.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not take cards, net banking or wallets on this website. Anyone
        asking you for card details, a PIN or an OTP in our name is not us.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Donations are non-refundable</h2>
      <p>
        Contributions are put to use immediately — fodder is bought, medicines
        are paid for, wages are met. Once a donation has been received it
        cannot be returned.
      </p>

      <h2>3. If something went wrong</h2>
      <p>These we will always look into:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Paid twice by mistake</strong> — tell us and we will return the duplicate</li>
        <li><strong>Money left your account but you got no acknowledgement</strong> — send us the transaction ID and we will trace it</li>
        <li><strong>Wrong amount entered</strong> — tell us within 7 days and we will discuss it with you</li>
        <li><strong>You did not make the payment at all</strong> — tell us at once</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a></strong>
          with your reference number (it begins <code>GOV</code>), the amount,
          the date, and the UPI transaction ID from your app. With those four
          things we can find your payment straight away.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>4. Failed and pending payments</h2>
      <p>
        If your UPI app shows the payment as failed but the money has left your
        account, it is with your bank, not with us — UPI normally reverses it
        within three to five working days. Raise it with your bank or in your
        UPI app first. If it has not come back after five working days, write
        to us and we will check our end.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Receipts</h2>
      <p>
        An 80G certificate is issued after we have verified your payment
        against our bank statement, and only if you asked for a receipt and
        gave a PAN. If you have not heard from us within 30 days, please chase
        us — quoting the reference number.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--t-lg); }
  .legal p, .legal li { color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.75; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .legal__meta {
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-block-end: var(--s-4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .legal .callout {
    background: var(--paper-warm);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--saffron);
    padding: var(--s-5);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }
  .legal .callout p { color: var(--ink); margin: 0; }
  .legal code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--surface-sunk);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
</style>
